From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] MMI: PROT3W, PEXEW, PEXCW, PEXEH, PEXCH move the right elements

What broke:
  The five one-source MMI permutes used the wrong SSE shuffles:
    PROT3W gave {w1, w2, w3, w0} instead of {w1, w2, w0, w3};
    PEXEW  gave {w2, w3, w0, w1} instead of {w2, w1, w0, w3};
    PEXCW  gave {w2, w3, w0, w1} instead of {w0, w2, w1, w3};
    PEXEH  gave {h2, h3, h0, h1} instead of {h2, h1, h0, h3} (per 64 bits);
    PEXCH  gave {h2, h3, h0, h1} instead of {h0, h2, h1, h3} (per 64 bits).
  Ben 10: Protector of Earth's software skinning (FUN_0015f198) packs two
  skinned vertices into 24 bytes with PROT3W + PEXTUW; with the wrong
  PROT3W every second vertex got its w (0) written as its x coordinate.

Why:
  The comments described other operations ("rotate left by 3", "swap 0<>2,
  1<>3") and the shuffles followed the comments.

The fix:
  New runtime macros PS2_PEXCH and PS2_PEXCW; PS2_PEXEH, PS2_PEXEW and
  PS2_PROT3W corrected (element orders documented next to them); the five
  translators use the macros.
  Sources: the EE Core Instruction Set Manual's definitions, and QEMU's
  target/mips tx79 implementation (PROT3W, PEXEW, PEXEH; PEXCH and PEXCW
  as described in its patch series).
  New ps2xTest case "MMI word and halfword permutes move the right
  elements" (fails before, passes after); "Unary MMI permutations read their
  source from rt" also checks that the translators use the macros.
  PREVH (reverses all 8 halfwords here; believed to reverse within each
  64-bit half) is not changed: not verified against a reference yet.

How it was found:
  findings/18 s.12: the vertices of the giant triangles in the first level
  came from a DMA buffer the game rewrites every frame; a hardware
  watchpoint on it stopped in FUN_0015f198, whose packing code showed the
  x = 0 pattern seen in the bad vertices.

--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
@@ -455,8 +455,9 @@
 
     std::string CodeGenerator::translatePEXEH(const Instruction &inst)
     {
-        // Swaps halfwords 1<->3 and 5<->7 within the 128-bit register
-        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_shufflelo_epi16(_mm_shufflehi_epi16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), _MM_SHUFFLE(2,3,0,1)), _MM_SHUFFLE(2,3,0,1)));",
+        // Parallel Exchange Even Halfword: in each 64-bit half, halfwords 0 and 2 swap and
+        // halfwords 1 and 3 stay (rd.h = {rt.h2, rt.h1, rt.h0, rt.h3} per half).
+        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PEXEH(GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));",
                            inst.rd, inst.rt);
     }
 
@@ -521,8 +522,9 @@
 
     std::string CodeGenerator::translatePROT3W(const Instruction &inst)
     {
-        // Rotates words left by 3: [d,c,b,a] -> [a,d,c,b]
-        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_shuffle_epi32(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), _MM_SHUFFLE(0,3,2,1)));",
+        // Parallel Rotate 3 Words: the three low words rotate, word 3 stays:
+        // rd = {w0: rt.w1, w1: rt.w2, w2: rt.w0, w3: rt.w3}.
+        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PROT3W(GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));",
                            inst.rd, inst.rt);
     }
 
@@ -561,8 +563,9 @@
 
     std::string CodeGenerator::translatePEXCH(const Instruction &inst)
     {
-        // Parallel Exchange Center Halfword (same as MMI2 PEXEH)
-        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_shufflelo_epi16(_mm_shufflehi_epi16(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), _MM_SHUFFLE(2,3,0,1)), _MM_SHUFFLE(2,3,0,1)));",
+        // Parallel Exchange Center Halfword: in each 64-bit half, halfwords 1 and 2 swap and
+        // halfwords 0 and 3 stay (rd.h = {rt.h0, rt.h2, rt.h1, rt.h3} per half).
+        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PEXCH(GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));",
                            inst.rd, inst.rt);
     }
 
@@ -578,8 +581,8 @@
 
     std::string CodeGenerator::translatePEXCW(const Instruction &inst)
     {
-        // Parallel Exchange Center Word (Swaps words 0<>2, 1<>3)
-        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, _mm_shuffle_epi32(GPR_VEC(ctx, {}), _MM_SHUFFLE(1,0,3,2)));",
+        // Parallel Exchange Center Word: words 1 and 2 swap, words 0 and 3 stay.
+        return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, PS2_PEXCW(GPR_VEC(ctx, {})));",
                            inst.rd, inst.rt);
     }
 
--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/ps2_runtime_macros.h
@@ -964,9 +964,18 @@
 }
 #define PS2_QFSRV(rs, rt, sa) ps2_qfsrv((__m128i)(rs), (__m128i)(rt), (uint32_t)(sa))
 #define PS2_PCPYLD(rs, rt) _mm_unpacklo_epi64(rt, rs)
-#define PS2_PEXEH(rs) _mm_shufflelo_epi16(_mm_shufflehi_epi16(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(2, 3, 0, 1)), _MM_SHUFFLE(2, 3, 0, 1))
-#define PS2_PEXEW(rs) _mm_shuffle_epi32(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(2, 3, 0, 1))
-#define PS2_PROT3W(rs) _mm_shuffle_epi32(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(0, 3, 2, 1))
+// MMI word/halfword permutes (EE Core Instruction Set Manual; element 0 = the lowest):
+//   PEXEH: per 64-bit half, halfwords 0 and 2 swap        -> {h2, h1, h0, h3}
+//   PEXCH: per 64-bit half, halfwords 1 and 2 swap        -> {h0, h2, h1, h3}
+//   PEXEW: words 0 and 2 swap                             -> {w2, w1, w0, w3}
+//   PEXCW: words 1 and 2 swap                             -> {w0, w2, w1, w3}
+//   PROT3W: the three low words rotate, word 3 stays      -> {w1, w2, w0, w3}
+// _MM_SHUFFLE lists the source element for lanes 3, 2, 1, 0 (highest first).
+#define PS2_PEXEH(rs) _mm_shufflelo_epi16(_mm_shufflehi_epi16(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 0, 1, 2)), _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 0, 1, 2))
+#define PS2_PEXCH(rs) _mm_shufflelo_epi16(_mm_shufflehi_epi16(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 1, 2, 0)), _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 1, 2, 0))
+#define PS2_PEXEW(rs) _mm_shuffle_epi32(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 0, 1, 2))
+#define PS2_PEXCW(rs) _mm_shuffle_epi32(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 1, 2, 0))
+#define PS2_PROT3W(rs) _mm_shuffle_epi32(rs, _MM_SHUFFLE(3, 0, 2, 1))
 
 // Additional VU0 operations
 #define PS2_VSQRT(x) sqrtf(x)
